Article 23 The directors, supervisors and senior officers appointed or recommended for appointment by the institution performing the functions of a contributor shall meet the following conditions:
(1) having good character;
(2) having the professional knowledge and work ability required for the position;
(3) having the physical condition to perform duties normally; and
(4) other conditions prescribed by laws and administrative regulations.
Where a director, supervisor or senior officer, during his or her term of office, falls under any circumstance that does not meet the conditions specified in the preceding paragraph, or falls under any circumstance specified in the Company Law of the People's Republic of China under which a person shall not serve as a director, supervisor or senior officer, the institution performing the functions of a contributor shall, according to law, remove him or her, or propose his or her removal.

Enterprise restructuring as referred to in this Law means:
(1) conversion of a wholly state-owned enterprise into a wholly state-owned company;
(2) conversion of a wholly state-owned enterprise or wholly state-owned company into a state-controlled company or a non-state-controlled company;
(3) conversion of a state-controlled company into a non-state-controlled company.

Without the consent of the institution performing the duties of a contributor, a wholly state-owned enterprise or wholly state-owned company shall not engage in any of the following acts:
(1) concluding an agreement on property transfer or loan with an affiliate;
(2) providing guarantee for an affiliate;
(3) making joint investment with an affiliate to establish an enterprise, or investing in an enterprise owned or actually controlled by a director, supervisor, senior officer, or their close relatives.

Article 59 The state capital operating budget shall be prepared for the following state capital incomes obtained by the State and for the expenditures of the following incomes:
(1) profits distributed from state-invested enterprises;
(2) income from the transfer of state-owned assets;
(3) liquidation income obtained from state-invested enterprises; and
(4) other state capital incomes.

Article 68 Where the institution performing the functions of a contributor commits any of the following acts, the persons directly in charge and other persons directly responsible shall be given sanctions according to law:
(1) appointing or recommending the appointment of managers of state-invested enterprises not in accordance with the statutory qualifications;
(2) misappropriating, intercepting or embezzling funds of state-invested enterprises or state capital revenues that shall be turned over;
(3) deciding on major matters of state-invested enterprises in violation of the statutory authority or procedures, thereby causing losses to state-owned assets; or
(4) having other acts of failing to perform the functions of a contributor according to law, thereby causing losses to state-owned assets.

Article 71 Where a director, supervisor, or senior officer of a state-invested enterprise commits any of the following acts, causing losses to state-owned assets, he or she shall bear compensation liability according to law; if he or she is a state functionary, disciplinary action shall also be taken according to law:
(1) Taking bribes or obtaining other illegal income or improper benefits by taking advantage of his or her position;
(2) Embezzling or misappropriating enterprise assets;
(3) In the process of enterprise restructuring, property transfer, etc., violating laws, administrative regulations, and fair transaction rules by transferring enterprise property at a low price or converting it into shares at a low price;
(4) Conducting transactions with this enterprise in violation of the provisions of this Law;
(5) Failing to truthfully provide relevant information and materials to asset appraisal institutions or accounting firms, or colluding with asset appraisal institutions or accounting firms to issue false asset appraisal reports or audit reports;
(6) Deciding on major matters of the enterprise in violation of the decision-making procedures stipulated by laws, administrative regulations, and the enterprise's articles of association;
(7) Other acts in the performance of duties that violate laws, administrative regulations, or the enterprise's articles of association.
The income obtained by a director, supervisor, or senior officer of a state-invested enterprise from the acts listed in the preceding paragraph shall be recovered according to law or shall belong to the state-invested enterprise.
Where a director, supervisor, or senior officer appointed or recommended for appointment by the institution performing the duties of a capital contributor commits any of the acts listed in the first paragraph of this Article, causing significant losses to state-owned assets, the institution performing the duties of a capital contributor shall remove him or her from office according to law or propose his or her removal from office.
